<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!-- A private map-mesh dirty flag, owned by this mod and subscribed to by exactly one layer
       (SectionLayer_SunShadows, via Patch_SunShadowAxisInvalidation).

       Why a whole new flag instead of reusing MapMeshFlagDefOf.Buildings: the sun-shadow mesh has
       to be rebuilt whenever the shadow AXIS moves far enough for its baked per-section length
       variation to go stale (DESIGN.md section 3), which happens ~720 times a game day. Raising
       `Buildings` that often would drag seven other section layers along with it — see the
       flag-to-layers table in DESIGN.md section 16 — for a change that can only ever affect this
       one. A dedicated flag reuses vanilla's own invalidation machinery (including its "only
       regenerate sections the camera can see" deferral) while touching nothing else.

       MapMeshFlagDef derives its bitmask from its def index (FlagDefUtility.SetMaskFromIndex), so
       this simply takes the next free bit after vanilla's 15. No label is needed: the flag is never
       shown to the player. -->
  <MapMeshFlagDef>
    <defName>CL_SunShadowAxis</defName>
  </MapMeshFlagDef>

</Defs>
